Supplementary Table 3. Associations observed at p<5x10-8 and variant features.	Unnamed: 1	Unnamed: 2	Unnamed: 3	Unnamed: 4	Unnamed: 5	Unnamed: 6	Unnamed: 7	Unnamed: 8	Unnamed: 9	Unnamed: 10	Unnamed: 11	Unnamed: 12	Unnamed: 13	Unnamed: 14	Unnamed: 15	Unnamed: 16	Unnamed: 17
C: Loci identified in previous studies																	
Associated variants from previous studies have been searched in the present study for corresponding immune traits. 																	
"Results have been considered as: ""confirmed"" if the top associated variant in the present study is suggestive (P<5x10-8) and it is the same of the previous study; ""confirmed and refined"" if the top associated variant in the present study is suggestive (P<5x10-8) but different from the previous study."																	
Other specific situations are indicated in column (I).																	
Association results in the present study have been obtained using a linear mixed model and the significant threshold obtained with a Bonferroni correction of the empirical threshold (P<6.9x10-9)6 for 538 independent tests (P<1.28x10-11).																	
																	
